troke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="240,113 231.8,116.8 231.8,109.2" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="252" y="113" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">v</text><line x1="28" y1="60" x2="28" y2="32.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="28,28 31,34.3 25,34.3" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="28" y="19" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">N</text><circle cx="30" cy="216" r="4.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="30" cy="216" r="1.6" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="42" y="216" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">B upwards (out of the page)</text></svg>', 'Top view with north up the page: a proton moving due east (to the right) through a uniform magnetic field pointing vertically upwards, out of the page.'),
('399fe610-bd91-59c4-9916-ce778332bc9f', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 22, 22, 'A proton and an α-particle move at the same speed at right angles to the same magnetic field. Calculate (force on α-particle) ÷ (force on proton).', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'F = BQv and the α-particle has charge 2e: ratio = 2 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ ÷ 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 2.0. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: F ∝ Q. A1: ratio = 2.0.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('5bbe837b-47a2-57db-914c-4238d3069542', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 23, 23, 'Which step links F = BIL to the force on a single moving charge, F = BQv?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'A charge Q moving at speed v forms a current I = Q/t over a length L = vt, so BIL = BQv', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'IL = (Q/t)(vt) = Qv. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: B (A charge Q moving at speed v forms a current I = Q/t over a length L = vt, so BIL = BQv).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('1a0b9082-7ec5-5148-970d-4c9daf4e0dc2', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 24, 24, 'An electron moves at 1.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹ at right angles to the Earth''s field of 5.0 × 10⁻⁵ T. Calculate the magnetic force on it, in units of 10⁻¹⁷ N. Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '8', '10⁻¹⁷ N', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'F = BQv = 5.0 × 10⁻⁵ × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 1.0 × 10⁷ = 8.00 × 10⁻¹⁷ N. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: F = BQv. A1: F = 8.0 × 10⁻¹⁷ N.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('ff6dd8d1-5c3b-50d7-9d16-63b73e895759', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 25, 25, 'A beam of neutrons passes through a strong magnetic field. What happens to the beam?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'It is not deflected, because neutrons are uncharged', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The magnetic force needs a charge: F = BQv with Q = 0. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: C (It is not deflected, because neutrons are uncharged).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('da4e215b-0b70-55bf-9092-3adac3cc1d5e', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 26, 26, 'In an old television tube, electrons moving at 3.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹ cross a deflecting field of 2.0 mT at right angles. Calculate the acceleration of an electron. Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C and mₑ = 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ kg.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.054e16', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'F = BQv = 2.0 × 10⁻³ × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 3.0 × 10⁷ = 9.60 × 10⁻¹⁵ N. a = F/m = 9.600 × 10⁻¹⁵ ÷ 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ = 1.05 × 10¹⁶ m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: F = BQv. C1: a = F/m. A1: a = 1.05 × 10¹⁶ m s⁻².', 3, NULL, NULL),
('673c4b1a-8903-5051-854d-9688fb1b167d', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 27, 27, 'Free electrons drift at 2.0 × 10⁻⁴ m s⁻¹ along a copper wire that lies at right angles to a 0.50 T field. Calculate the magnetic force on one electron, in units of 10⁻²³ N. Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.6', '10⁻²³ N', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'F = BQv = 0.50 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 2.0 × 10⁻⁴ = 1.60 × 10⁻²³ N: tiny, but there are about 10²² free electrons in each centimetre of wire. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: F = Bev. C1: substitution. A1: F = 1.6 × 10⁻²³ N.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('67c86dc5-95c2-5b23-a170-f4be8d355e03', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 28, 28, 'A proton and an electron move in the same direction at the same speed through the same magnetic field. How do the magnetic forces on them compare?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Equal in size and opposite in direction', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'F = BQv: same |Q|, v and B; the sign of Q reverses the direction. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: same |Q|. C1: opposite sign gives opposite force. A1: A (Equal in size and opposite in direction).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('2d727d43-86e4-574c-9961-5cda8a44e5a5', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 29, 29, 'A charged dust grain of mass 1.0 × 10⁻¹² kg carries 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁵ C and moves at 50 m s⁻¹ at right angles to a field of 0.40 T. Calculate its acceleration due to the magnetic force.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.032', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'F = BQv = 0.40 × 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁵ × 50 = 3.2 × 10⁻¹⁴ N. a = F/m = 3.2 × 10⁻¹⁴ ÷ 1.0 × 10⁻¹² = 0.032 m s⁻². Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: F = BQv. C1: a = F/m. B1: magnetic effect tiny for a slow, heavy grain. A1: a = 0.032 m s⁻².', 4, NULL, NULL),
('6b389ac8-3a52-5f1e-a025-5be7d135ab27', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 30, 30, 'With speed 5.0 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹, an electron crosses a 0.10 T field at 40° to the field lines. Find the magnetic force on it, in units of 10⁻¹⁴ N. Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '5.142', '10⁻¹⁴ N', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'F = BQv sin θ = 0.10 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 5.0 × 10⁶ × sin 40° = 5.14 × 10⁻¹⁴ N. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: F = BQv sin θ. C1: substitution. A1: F = 5.14 × 10⁻¹⁴ N.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 340 230" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgbf89debe-t fgbf89debe-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgbf89debe-t">Electron at an angle to the field</title><desc id="fgbf89debe-d">Horizontal field lines of flux density 0.10 T; an electron moves at 5.0 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹ at 40° to the field lines.</desc><line x1="20" y1="30" x2="315.1" y2="30" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="320,30 313.7,33 313.7,27" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="20" y1="70" x2="315.1" y2="70" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="320,70 313.7,73 313.7,67" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="20" y1="110" x2="315.1" y2="110" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="320,110 313.7,113 313.7,107" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="20" y1="150" x2="315.1" y2="150" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="320,150 313.7,153 313.7,147" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="20" y1="190" x2="315.1" y2="190" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="320,190 313.7,193 313.7,187" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><text x="318" y="14" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8)">B = 0.10 T</text><circle cx="110" cy="150" r="9" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="110" cy="150" r="2.4" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="118.4" y1="142.9" x2="204.8" y2="70.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="209.6,66.4 205.8,74.6 200.9,68.8" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="217.2" y="50" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">v = 5.0 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹</text><line x1="110" y1="150" x2="200" y2="150" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:4 3"/><path d="M160,150 A50,50 0 0,0 148.3,117.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="170.1" y="128.1" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">40°</text><text x="94" y="132" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">electron</text></svg>', 'Horizontal field lines of flux density 0.10 T; an electron moves at 5.0 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹ at 40° to the field lines.'),
('47964ae1-f4e8-53eb-9fb8-f0b1b58a5c73', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 31, 31, 'A charged particle enters a uniform magnetic field with its velocity at an acute angle to the field lines. What is the shape of its path?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'A helix (spiral) along the field lines', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The perpendicular velocity component gives circular motion; the parallel component carries it along the field. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: components of velocity. C1: circle plus drift gives helix. A1: D (A helix (spiral) along the field lines).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('2794185d-cbd4-51e2-9eff-8600dc8cd4e8', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 32, 32, 'At what speed must a proton move at right angles to a 0.10 T field to feel a magnetic force of 1.0 × 10⁻¹³ N? Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '6.25e6', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = F/(BQ) = 1.0 × 10⁻¹³ ÷ (0.10 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 6.25 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: rearranged. C1: substitution. A1: v = 6.25 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('a9931ff0-860b-581c-b376-1af051974034', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 33, 33, 'An electron is accelerated from rest through 500 V and then moves at right angles to a field of 0.010 T. Calculate the magnetic force on it, in units of 10⁻¹⁴ N. Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C and mₑ = 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ kg.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.12', '10⁻¹⁴ N', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = √(2eV/m) = √(2 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 500 ÷ 9.11 × 10⁻³¹) = 1.33 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹. F = BQv = 0.010 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 1.325 × 10⁷ = 2.12 × 10⁻¹⁴ N. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: ½mv² = eV. C1: speed. C1: F = BQv. A1: F = 2.12 × 10⁻¹⁴ N.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('7698bd80-6cf0-53b7-a8cc-c3df7125bc26', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 34, 34, 'Why are auroras seen mainly near the Earth''s magnetic poles?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Charged particles from the Sun spiral along the field lines, which converge and enter the atmosphere near the poles', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Motion along the field is unaffected, so particles follow the field lines down near the poles. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: spiral along field lines. C1: lines enter atmosphere near poles. A1: B (Charged particles from the Sun spiral along the field lines, which converge and enter the atmosphere near the poles).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('6d4e6de5-fd84-5393-ac5f-add7710944b6', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 35, 35, 'An ion moving at 2.0 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹ at right angles to a 0.50 T field feels a force of 3.2 × 10⁻¹⁴ N. Calculate its charge, as a multiple of e. Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Q = F/(Bv) = 3.2 × 10⁻¹⁴ ÷ (0.50 × 2.0 × 10⁵) = 3.2 × 10⁻¹⁹ C, and 3.2 × 10⁻¹⁹ ÷ 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 2.0. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: Q = F/(Bv). C1: ÷ e. A1: Q/e = 2.0.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('84434522-a263-52ec-ab93-25679563cf49', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 36, 36, 'The charge of a particle is doubled and its speed is halved, in the same field. What happens to the magnetic force on it?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'It stays the same', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'F = BQv: doubling Q and halving v leaves the product Qv, and so F, unchanged. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: F ∝ Qv. C1: product unchanged. C1: same field. A1: C (It stays the same).', 4, NULL, NULL),
('1e35e5f6-b0da-517e-b87a-b5b77eaedde5', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 37, 37, 'A charged particle feels half the maximum possible magnetic force for its speed. Calculate the angle between its velocity and the field.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '30', '°', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'sin θ = 0.50, so θ = sin⁻¹ 0.50 = 30°. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: F = F_max sin θ. C1: inverse sine. A1: θ = 30°.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('62020a8f-e050-5a72-a25d-aeb7beb2fbcb', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 38, 38, 'A singly charged ion moves at 4.0 × 10⁴ m s⁻¹ at right angles to a 0.60 T field in a mass spectrometer. Calculate the magnetic force on it, in units of 10⁻¹⁵ N. Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3.84', '10⁻¹⁵ N', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'F = BQv = 0.60 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 4.0 × 10⁴ = 3.84 × 10⁻¹⁵ N. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: F = BQv. C1: substitution. A1: F = 3.84 × 10⁻¹⁵ N.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('75ba8a70-dccc-5693-95c0-03fa8d5f21c1', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 39, 39, 'Several beams pass at right angles through a magnetic field. Which beam is NOT deflected?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'A beam of neutrons', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Neutrons carry no charge. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: force needs charge. C1: neutrons neutral. A1: A (A beam of neutrons).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('0818c296-35a3-5777-80a9-d40ce722b3be', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 40, 40, 'An electron moves at 2.0 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹ at right angles to a field of 3.0 mT. Calculate its acceleration. Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C and mₑ = 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ kg.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.054e15', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'F = BQv = 3.0 × 10⁻³ × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 2.0 × 10⁶ = 9.60 × 10⁻¹⁶ N. a = 9.600 × 10⁻¹⁶ ÷ 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ = 1.05 × 10¹⁵ m s⁻². Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: field in T. C1: F = BQv. C1: a = F/m. A1: a = 1.05 × 10¹⁵ m s⁻².', 4, NULL, NULL),
('59d18be4-82d4-55b6-8a2b-11f625f248f4', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 41, 41, 'An electron moves due north in a magnetic field that points vertically downwards. In which direction is the force on it?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Due east', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Conventional current is due south; left-hand rule with first finger down and second finger south gives a thumb pointing east. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: current opposite to electron velocity. C1: left-hand rule. A1: D (Due east).', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 230" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgd838ca11-t fgd838ca11-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgd838ca11-t">Electron in a vertical field</title><desc id="fgd838ca11-d">Top view with north up the page: an electron moving due north through a uniform magnetic field pointing vertically downwards, into the page.</desc><line x1="42.2" y1="32.6" x2="50.2" y2="40.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="42.2" y1="40.6" x2="50.2" y2="32.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="42.2" y1="65.8" x2="50.2" y2="73.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="42.2" y1="73.8" x2="50.2" y2="65.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="42.2" y1="99" x2="50.2" y2="107" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="42.2" y1="107" x2="50.2" y2="99" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-wid