('89313f6e-62de-5d3f-ab9e-bd173761af00', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', 'ca14c791-7996-5cb6-9fb9-b8764146fc83', 'a-level', '25.1', '9702 coursebook 25.1 · Force on a moving charge', 48, 48, 'In a mass spectrometer, a singly charged ion of mass 4.0 × 10⁻²⁶ kg moves at 1.0 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹ at right angles to a field of 0.10 T. (a) Calculate the magnetic force. (b) Calculate its weight. (c) Calculate (magnetic force) ÷ (weight) and comment. Give only the ratio. Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C and g = 9.81 m s⁻².', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '4.077e9', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) F = 0.10 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 1.0 × 10⁵ = 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁵ N. (b) W = 4.0 × 10⁻²⁶ × 9.81 = 3.92 × 10⁻²⁵ N. (c) Ratio = 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁵ ÷ 3.924 × 10⁻²⁵ = 4.08 × 10⁹: gravity is completely negligible. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: F = BQv. C1: W = mg. C1: ratio. B1: gravity negligible. A1: ratio = 4.08 × 10⁹.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 260" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg570f12b1-t fg570f12b1-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg570f12b1-t">Mass spectrometer</title><desc id="fg570f12b1-d">A singly charged ion of mass 4.0 × 10⁻²⁶ kg enters a uniform 0.10 T field (out of the page) through a slit at 1.0 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹ and travels a semicircle to the detector.</desc><rect x="60" y="20" width="340" height="180" rx="0" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/><circle cx="77" cy="38" r="4.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="77" cy="38" r="1.6" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><circle cx="77" cy="74" r="4.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="77" cy="74" r