('db34e078-2898-57e6-952f-1aeb01515b4e', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '9a577035-5226-4d06-b1f8-39a2b1f93b0a', 'a-level', '25.2', '9702 coursebook 25.2 · Orbiting charged particles', 25, 25, 'A proton moves in a circle of radius 0.30 m in a 0.50 T field. Calculate its kinetic energy, in MeV (1 MeV = 1.6 × 10⁻¹³ J). Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C and mₚ = 1.67 × 10⁻²⁷ kg.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.078', 'MeV', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'p = BQr = 0.50 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 0.30 = 2.4 × 10⁻²⁰ kg m s⁻¹. E_k = p²/2m = (2.4 × 10⁻²⁰)² ÷ (2 × 1.67 × 10⁻²⁷) = 1.72 × 10⁻¹³ J. In MeV: 1.725 × 10⁻¹³ ÷ 1.6 × 10⁻¹³ = 1.08. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: p = BQr. C1: E_k = p²/2m. A1: E_k = 1.08 MeV.', 3, NULL, NULL),
