('6609c2d4-e079-5783-936a-431e3c8fbdcd', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '9a577035-5226-4d06-b1f8-39a2b1f93b0a', 'a-level', '25.2', '9702 coursebook 25.2 · Orbiting charged particles', 32, 32, 'In a cloud chamber in a magnetic field, a charged particle''s track is a spiral of decreasing radius. Why?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The particle loses kinetic energy by ionising the gas, so its speed and radius decrease', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'r = mv/BQ, and v falls as energy is lost in collisions. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: energy lost to ionisation. C1: r ∝ v. A1: D (The particle loses kinetic energy by ionising the gas, so its speed and radius decrease).', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 260" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgcd1b73cc-t fgcd1b73cc-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgcd1b73cc-t">Spiral track</title><desc id="fgcd1b73cc-d">A charged particle track in a cloud chamber in a uniform field into the page: a spiral whose radius decreases as the particle moves.</desc><line x1="30" y1="27.5" x2="38" y2="35.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="30" y1="35.5" x2="38" y2="27.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="30" y1="62.5" x2="38" y2="70.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="30" y1="70.5" x2="38" y2="62.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="30" y1="97.5" x2="38" y2="105.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="30" y1="105.5" x2="38" y2="97.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7