('c21389f3-4776-5638-81df-885ac3968bb5', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '9a577035-5226-4d06-b1f8-39a2b1f93b0a', 'a-level', '25.2', '9702 coursebook 25.2 · Orbiting charged particles', 44, 44, 'A cyclotron for protons has dees of radius 0.40 m in a field of 1.2 T. Each time a proton crosses the gap between the dees it gains 20 keV. (a) Calculate the maximum speed of the protons. (b) Calculate their maximum kinetic energy, in MeV. (c) Calculate the number of complete revolutions a proton makes. Give only the answer to (c). Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C and mₚ = 1.67 × 10⁻²⁷ kg.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '275.9', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) v = BQr/m = 1.2 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 0.40 ÷ 1.67 × 10⁻²⁷ = 4.60 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹. (b) E_k = 0.5 × 1.67 × 10⁻²⁷ × (4.599 × 10⁷)² = 1.77 × 10⁻¹² J, which is 11.0 MeV. (c) Two crossings per revolution give 40 keV, so n = 1.766 × 10⁻¹² ÷ (2 × 20 × 10³ × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 276. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: v = BQr/m. C1: ½mv². C1: conversion to MeV. M1: two gap crossings per revolution. C1: number of revolutions. A1: n = 276.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 360 310" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg139d4b3a-t fg139d4b3a-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg139d4b3a-t">Cyclotron</title><desc id="fg139d4b3a-d">Top view of a proton cyclotron: two D-shaped dees of radius 0.40 m in a 1.2 T field out of the page; each crossing of the gap adds 20 keV, and the protons spiral outwards.</desc><path d="M172,25 A105,105 0 0,0 172,235 Z" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M188,25 A105,105 0 0,1 188,235 Z" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polyline points="180,118 180.2,117.9 180.4,117.8 180.6,117.7 180.9,117.6 1