('baff7ea6-4c19-5b39-8b79-4cc9fc4eca9a', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '9a577035-5226-4d06-b1f8-39a2b1f93b0a', 'a-level', '25.2', '9702 coursebook 25.2 · Orbiting charged particles', 45, 45, 'An electron track in a field of 2.0 mT has a radius of 5.0 cm at first and 3.0 cm later, after the electron has lost energy. (a) Show that the kinetic energy is (BQr)²/2m. (b) Calculate the initial kinetic energy, in eV. (c) Calculate the energy lost, in eV. Give only the answer to (c). Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C and mₑ = 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ kg.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '562', 'eV', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) p = mv = BQr, so E_k = p²/2m = (BQr)²/2m. (b) E₁ = (2.0 × 10⁻³ × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 0.050)² ÷ (2 × 9.11 × 10⁻³¹) = 1.41 × 10⁻¹⁶ J, which is 878 eV. (c) E ∝ r², so E₂ = 0.36E₁ and the loss = 0.64 × 878.2 = 562 eV. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: E_k = (BQr)²/2m. C1: initial energy. C1: E ∝ r². C1: energy lost. A1: ΔE = 562 eV.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 260" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg0be58d7d-t fg0be58d7d-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg0be58d7d-t">Electron losing energy</title><desc id="fg0be58d7d-d">An electron track in a uniform 2.0 mT field directed out of the page: a spiral whose radius shrinks from 5.0 cm at first to 3.0 cm later as the electron loses energy.</desc><circle cx="34" cy="31.5" r="4.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="34" cy="31.5" r="1.6" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><circle cx="34" cy="66.5" r="4.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="34" cy="66.5" r="1.6" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><circle cx="34" cy="101.5" r="4.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill