('a423a0a7-d890-5e2e-87ee-5fcf643855c2', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '9a577035-5226-4d06-b1f8-39a2b1f93b0a', 'a-level', '25.2', '9702 coursebook 25.2 · Orbiting charged particles', 46, 46, 'Electrons moving at 2.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹ enter a region 2.0 cm wide containing a uniform field of 2.0 mT at right angles to their motion. (a) Calculate the radius of their circular path in the field. (b) Show that the angle θ through which they are deflected satisfies sin θ = (width)/r. (c) Calculate θ. Give only the answer to (c). Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C and mₑ = 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ kg.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '20.56', '°', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) r = 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ × 2.0 × 10⁷ ÷ (1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 2.0 × 10⁻³) = 0.0569 m. (b) The electron follows an arc of radius r; geometry of the arc across width d gives sin θ = d/r. (c) sin θ = 0.020 ÷ 0.05694 = 0.3513, so θ = sin⁻¹ 0.3513 = 20.6°. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: r = mv/BQ. B1: geometry sin θ = d/r. C1: sin θ value. C1: θ. B1: speed unchanged. A1: θ = 20.6°.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 240" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgb264ba80-t fgb264ba80-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgb264ba80-t">Beam crossing a field region</title><desc id="fgb264ba80-d">Electrons moving at 2.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹ enter a region 2.0 cm wide containing a uniform 2.0 mT field at right angles to their motion; inside, they move on a circular arc and leave deflected.</desc><rect x="150" y="14" width="110" height="190" rx="0" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/><line x1="164.3" y1="25.8" x2="172.3" y2="33.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="164.3" y1="33.8" x2="172.3" y2="25.8" style="stroke:var(--f