,81 178.1,81.3 180.9,81.5 183.7,81.8 186.4,82.1 189.2,82.5 192,82.8 194.8,83.2 197.6,83.6 200.4,84.1 203.1,84.5 205.9,85 208.7,85.5 211.4,86.1 214.2,86.6 216.9,87.2 219.7,87.8 222.4,88.5 225.1,89.1 227.9,89.8 230.6,90.5 233.3,91.3 236,92 238.7,92.8 241.4,93.6 244.1,94.5 246.7,95.3 249.4,96.2 252.1,97.1 254.7,98 257.4,99 260,100" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="260" y1="100" x2="338.4" y2="129.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:6 4"/><polygon points="344.3,131.6 335.3,132.3 338,125.1" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><line x1="260" y1="100" x2="340" y2="100" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:3 3"/><polygon points="150,214 156.3,211 156.3,217" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="154.9" y1="214" x2="255.1" y2="214" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="260,214 253.7,217 253.7,211" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="205" y="225" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2.0 cm</text><text x="20" y="226" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">B = 2.0 mT</text></svg>', 'Electrons moving at 2.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹ enter a region 2.0 cm wide containing a uniform 2.0 mT field at right angles to their motion; inside, they move on a circular arc and leave deflected.'),
('adcce1ad-b6ba-5fef-933c-81db72069f41', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '9a577035-5226-4d06-b1f8-39a2b1f93b0a', 'a-level', '25.2', '9702 coursebook 25.2 · Orbiting charged particles', 47, 47, '(a) Show that the period of a charged particle in a uniform magnetic field is T = 2πm/BQ and is independent of its speed. (b) Calculate the period of a deuteron (mass 3.34 × 10⁻²⁷ kg, charge e) in a field of 1.5 T, in ns. Give only the answer to (b). Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '87.44 ns', 'ns', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) T = 2πr/v and r = mv/BQ, so T = 2πm/BQ: v cancels. (b) T = 2π × 3.34 × 10⁻²⁷ ÷ (1.5 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 8.74 × 10⁻⁸ s. In ns: 8.744 × 10⁻⁸ × 10⁹ = 87.4. Mark scheme (5 marks). M1: T = 2πr/v. B1: v cancels. C1: substitution. C1: conversion. A1: T = 87.4 ns.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('5604dccc-b91f-570a-aecb-31067eabc1b7', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '9a577035-5226-4d06-b1f8-39a2b1f93b0a', 'a-level', '25.2', '9702 coursebook 25.2 · Orbiting charged particles', 48, 48, 'In a fine-beam tube, electrons are accelerated through different p.d.s V and circle in a fixed field of 1.0 mT. Results: V/V = 100, 200, 300, 400 and r/cm = 3.37, 4.77, 5.84, 6.74. (a) Show that r² = 2mV/(eB²). (b) Calculate the gradient of a graph of r² against V using the first and last points. (c) Calculate e/m, in units of 10¹¹ C kg⁻¹. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.761', '10¹¹ C kg⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) r = √(2mV/e)/B, so r² = 2mV/(eB²). (b) Gradient = (0.0674² − 0.0337²) ÷ (400 − 100) = 1.14 × 10⁻⁵ m² V⁻¹. (c) e/m = 2 ÷ (B² × gradient) = 2 ÷ ((1.0 × 10⁻³)² × 1.136 × 10⁻⁵) = 1.76 × 10¹¹ C kg⁻¹. Mark scheme (6 marks). B1: r² expression. C1: r in m. C1: gradient. M1: e/m = 2/(B² × gradient). C1: value. A1: e/m = 1.76 × 10¹¹ C kg⁻¹.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 410" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgbdfefd41-t fgbdfefd41-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgbdfefd41-t">Radius against accelerating p.d.</title><desc id="fgbdfefd41-d">Table and graph of the radius of the electron circle against accelerating p.d. at 1.0 mT: V = 100, 200, 300, 400 V give r = 3.37, 4.77, 5.84, 6.74 cm, plotted as points on a rising curve.</desc><g transform="translate(0,0)"><rect x="136.7" y="8" width="126.5" height="140" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="136.7" y="8" width="126.5" height="28" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="166.1" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">V / V</text><text x="229.4" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">r / cm</text><line x1="195.4" y1="8" x2="195.4" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136.7" y1="36" x2="263.3" y2="36" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="166.1" y="50" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">100</text><text x="229.4" y="50" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">3.37</text><line x1="136.7" y1="64" x2="263.3" y2="64" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="166.1" y="78" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">200</text><text x="229.4" y="78" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4.77</text><line x1="136.7" y1="92" x2="263.3" y2="92" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="166.1" y="106" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">300</text><text x="229.4" y="106" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">5.84</text><line x1="136.7" y1="120" x2="263.3" y2="120" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="166.1" y="134" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">400</text><text x="229.4" y="134" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">6.74</text></g><g transform="translate(0,160)"><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="109.2" y1="34" x2="109.2" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="194.5" y1="34" x2="194.5" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="279.7" y1="34" x2="279.7" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="365" y1="34" x2="365" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="202" x2="382" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="157.2" x2="382" y2="157.2" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="112.4" x2="382" y2="112.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="67.6" x2="382" y2="67.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="202" x2="388" y2="202" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="202" x2="24" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,202 385.7,205 385.7,199" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="24,24 27,30.3 21,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="24" y1="202" x2="24" y2="206" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="24" y="214" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="109.2" y1="202" x2="109.2" y2="206" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="109.2" y="214" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">100</text><line x1="194.5" y1="202" x2="194.5" y2="206" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="194.5" y="214" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">200</text><line x1="279.7" y1="202" x2="279.7" y2="206" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="279.7" y="214" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">300</text><line x1="365" y1="202" x2="365" y2="206" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="365" y="214" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">400</text><line x1="20" y1="202" x2="24" y2="202" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="202" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="20" y1="157.2" x2="24" y2="157.2" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="157.2" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2</text><line x1="20" y1="112.4" x2="24" y2="112.4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="112.4" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4</text><line x1="20" y1="67.6" x2="24" y2="67.6" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="67.6" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">6</text><text x="203" y="234" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">V / V</text><text x="20" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">r / cm</text><line x1="105.2" y1="122.5" x2="113.2" y2="130.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="105.2" y1="130.5" x2="113.2" y2="122.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="190.5" y1="91.2" x2="198.5" y2="99.2" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="190.5" y1="99.2" x2="198.5" y2="91.2" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="275.7" y1="67.2" x2="283.7" y2="75.2" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="275.7" y1="75.2" x2="283.7" y2="67.2" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="361" y1="47" x2="369" y2="55" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="361" y1="55" x2="369" y2="47" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></g></svg>', 'Table and graph of the radius of the electron circle against accelerating p.d. at 1.0 mT: V = 100, 200, 300, 400 V give r = 3.37, 4.77, 5.84, 6.74 cm, plotted as points on a rising curve.'),
('02de7cd1-ca76-5d28-8745-46582b9b9257', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '9a577035-5226-4d06-b1f8-39a2b1f93b0a', 'a-level', '25.2', '9702 coursebook 25.2 · Orbiting charged particles', 49, 49, 'A proton from the solar wind moves at 4.0 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹ at right angles to the Earth''s field of 3.0 × 10⁻⁵ T. (a) Calculate the radius of its circular path. (b) Calculate its period, in ms. (c) Explain why this traps the proton near the Earth. Give only the answer to (b). Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C and mₚ = 1.67 × 10⁻²⁷ kg.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.186 ms', 'ms', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) r = 1.67 × 10⁻²⁷ × 4.0 × 10⁵ ÷ (1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 3.0 × 10⁻⁵) = 139 m. (b) T = 2π × 1.67 × 10⁻²⁷ ÷ (1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 3.0 × 10⁻⁵) = 0.00219 s. In ms: 0.002186 × 1000 = 2.19. (c) It circles about the field lines instead of travelling straight on, so it stays in the magnetosphere. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: r = mv/BQ. C1: T = 2πm/BQ. C1: conversion. B1: trapped circling field lines. A1: T = 2.19 ms.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('86599d89-1ab6-5407-910a-07220cbbdc65', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '9a577035-5226-4d06-b1f8-39a2b1f93b0a', 'a-level', '25.2', '9702 coursebook 25.2 · Orbiting charged particles', 50, 50, 'An electron and a positron, each with a kinetic energy of 1.0 keV, move at right angles to a field of 1.0 mT. (a) Show that r = √(2mE_k)/(eB). (b) Calculate the radius of each path, in cm. (c) Explain how their tracks differ. Give only the answer to (b). Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C and mₑ = 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ kg.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '10.67 cm', 'cm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) p = √(2mE_k) and r = p/(eB). (b) E_k = 1.0 × 10³ × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁶ J; r = √(2 × 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ × 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁶) ÷ (1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 1.0 × 10⁻³) = 0.107 m. In cm: 0.1067 × 100 = 10.7. (c) Same radius, but they curve in opposite senses because their charges are opposite. Mark scheme (6 marks). B1: r from momentum. C1: keV to J. C1: radius. C1: conversion. B1: opposite curvature. A1: r = 10.7 cm.', 6, NULL, NULL)
