 m s⁻¹</text><line x1="120" y1="105" x2="350" y2="105" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:6 4"/><polygon points="356,105 348.7,108.4 348.7,101.6" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><polygon points="374,50 377,56.3 371,56.3" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="374" y1="54.9" x2="374" y2="155.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="374,160 371,153.7 377,153.7" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="380" y="105" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">8.0 mm</text><line x1="120" y1="194" x2="128" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="120" y1="202" x2="128" y2="194" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="136" y="198" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">B = 0.040 T</text></svg>', 'A velocity selector with plates 8.0 mm apart and a magnetic field of 0.040 T into the page, selecting ions of speed 5.0 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹.'),
('6b31872c-00bc-5336-b19c-ab1fe9f1ac18', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 18, 18, 'In a velocity selector, which force acts on a charged particle even when it is not moving?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The electric force', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'F = EQ needs no motion; F = BQv is zero when v = 0. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: A (The electric force).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('b1b064cc-6591-5c32-bc1f-3c2049f55423', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 19, 19, 'Calculate E/B for E = 1.0 × 10³ V m⁻¹ and B = 1.0 × 10⁻³ T.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1e6', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'E/B = 1.0 × 10³ ÷ 1.0 × 10⁻³ = 1.0 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (1 mark). A1: v = 1.0 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹.', 1, NULL, NULL),
('07d5a649-b1ac-56a4-83f7-43227625ac77', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 20, 20, 'How do the electric and magnetic forces on a charged particle depend on its speed?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The electric force does not depend on speed; the magnetic force is proportional to speed', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'F_E = EQ; F_B = BQv. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: D (The electric force does not depend on speed; the magnetic force is proportional to speed).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('a0e46ec8-24e1-5526-96ce-0bf4f7f49824', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 21, 21, 'A particle moves through a velocity selector at twice the selected speed. Calculate (magnetic force) ÷ (electric force).', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'At the selected speed BQv = EQ. For example, with E = 1.0 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹ and B = 0.010 T the selected speed is 1.0 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹; at 2.0 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹, F_B ÷ F_E = 0.010 × 2.0 × 10⁶ ÷ 1.0 × 10⁴ = 2.0. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: F_B ∝ v. A1: ratio = 2.0.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('0b864fda-5e3a-5616-a6a4-58340c986692', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 22, 22, 'The plate separation in a velocity selector is doubled, with the same p.d. and magnetic field. What happens to the speed selected?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'It halves', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'E = V/d halves, so v = E/B halves. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: B (It halves).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('5dc49a12-f006-52e4-b588-ea13a6e325ed', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 23, 23, 'A velocity selector has E = 2.0 × 10⁵ V m⁻¹ and B = 0.40 T. Calculate the kinetic energy of the protons it selects, in keV. Take mₚ = 1.67 × 10⁻²⁷ kg and e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.305', 'keV', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = E/B = 2.0 × 10⁵ ÷ 0.40 = 5.0 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹. E_k = 0.5 × 1.67 × 10⁻²⁷ × (5.0 × 10⁵)² = 2.09 × 10⁻¹⁶ J. In keV: 2.088 × 10⁻¹⁶ ÷ 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁶ = 1.30. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: v = E/B then ½mv². A1: E_k = 1.30 keV.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('9bfd83bc-4210-52a0-91f4-cb0035343ffc', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 24, 24, 'A velocity selector has plates 10 mm apart with a p.d. of 500 V and a magnetic field of 0.10 T. Calculate the speed selected.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '5e5', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'E = 500 ÷ 0.010 = 5.0 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹. v = E/B = 5.0 × 10⁴ ÷ 0.10 = 5.0 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: E = V/d. C1: v = E/B. A1: v = 5.0 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 440 242" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg417ac162-t fg417ac162-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg417ac162-t">Velocity selector</title><desc id="fg417ac162-d">A velocity selector with plates 10 mm apart, a p.d. of 500 V between them and a magnetic field of 0.10 T into the page.</desc><rect x="120" y="42" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="120" y="160" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="108" y="46" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">+</text><text x="108" y="164" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">−</text><line x1="139.3" y1="68.3" x2="147.3" y2="76.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="139.3" y1="76.3" x2="147.3" y2="68.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="139.3" y1="133.7" x2="14