('8846830c-70de-5b0e-9cec-2fadb2f951b0', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 25, 25, 'Electrons accelerated from rest through 2.0 kV enter crossed fields with B = 1.0 mT. The plates are 1.0 cm apart. Calculate the p.d. across the plates needed for the electrons to pass undeflected. Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C and mₑ = 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ kg.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '265.1', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = √(2 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 2000 ÷ 9.11 × 10⁻³¹) = 2.65 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹. E = Bv = 1.0 × 10⁻³ × 2.651 × 10⁷ = 2.65 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹. V = Ed = 2.651 × 10⁴ × 0.010 = 265 V. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: speed. C1: E = Bv. C1: V = Ed. A1: V = 265 V.', 4, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 440 222" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg0934f40b-t fg0934f40b-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg0934f40b-t">Crossed fields for electrons</title><desc id="fg0934f40b-d">Electrons accelerated through 2.0 kV enter crossed fields: plates 1.0 cm apart and a magnetic field of 1.0 mT. The top plate is positive and the magnetic field points into the page.</desc><rect x="120" y="42" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="120" y="160" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="108" y="46" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">+</text><text x="108" y="164" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">−</text><line x1="139.3" y1="68.3" x2="147.3" y2="76.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b728