('d216a42f-9c58-50d4-a1a0-8a0740de3dea', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 31, 31, 'In a Bainbridge mass spectrometer, a selector with E = 1.0 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹ and B₁ = 0.050 T is followed by a field B₂ = 0.050 T. Singly charged ions follow a circle of radius 0.083 m. Calculate the mass of an ion, in units of 10⁻²⁷ kg. Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3.32', '10⁻²⁷ kg', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = E/B₁ = 1.0 × 10⁴ ÷ 0.050 = 2.0 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹. m = QB₂r/v = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 0.050 × 0.083 ÷ 2.0 × 10⁵ = 3.32 × 10⁻²⁷ kg. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: v = E/B₁. M1: m = QB₂r/v. C1: value. A1: m = 3.32 × 10⁻²⁷ kg.', 4, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 260" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgb07a88bb-t fgb07a88bb-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgb07a88bb-t">Bainbridge mass spectrometer</title><desc id="fgb07a88bb-d">Ions leaving a velocity selector (E = 1.0 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹, B₁ = 0.050 T) enter a field B₂ = 0.050 T and travel a semicircle of radius 0.083 m to the detector.</desc><rect x="60" y="20" width="340" height="180" rx="0" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/><circle cx="77" cy="38" r="4.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="77" cy="38" r="1.6" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><circle cx="77" cy="74" r="4.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="77" cy="74" r="1.6" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><circle cx="77" cy="110" r="4.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke