('3d762e45-665e-5d8b-9e85-e614927424aa', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 32, 32, 'Both E and B in a velocity selector are doubled. What happens to the speed of the particles that pass through?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'It is unchanged', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = E/B; doubling both leaves the ratio unchanged, though the forces are larger. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: v = E/B. C1: ratio unchanged. C1: forces larger but balanced. A1: D (It is unchanged).', 4, NULL, NULL),
('5af89d3d-7597-550d-9369-117d96765f9e', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 33, 33, 'An electron moving at 1.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹ passes between plates 4.0 cm long where the electric field is 2.0 × 10³ V m⁻¹ (no magnetic field). Calculate its sideways deflection, in mm. Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C and mₑ = 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ kg.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.81 mm', 'mm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a = eE/m = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 2.0 × 10³ ÷ 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ = 3.51 × 10¹⁴ m s⁻². t = 0.040 ÷ 1.0 × 10⁷ = 4.0 × 10⁻⁹ s. y = ½at² = 0.5 × 3.513 × 10¹⁴ × (4.0 × 10⁻⁹)² = 0.00281 m. In mm: 0.002810 × 1000 = 2.81. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: a and t. C1: y = ½at². A1: y = 2.81 mm.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 220" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgb672c917-t fgb672c917-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgb672c917-t">Electron between plates</title><desc id="fgb672c917-d">An electron moving at 1.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹ enters midway between parallel plates 4.0 cm long with a field of 2.0 × 10³ V m⁻¹; it is deflected towards the positive plate.</desc><rect x="90" y="42" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="90" y="170" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="78" y="46" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">+</text><text x="78" y="174" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">−</text><line x1="110" y1="56" x2="110" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke