e="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="243.3" y1="141.7" x2="251.3" y2="133.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="278" y1="68.3" x2="286" y2="76.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="278" y1="76.3" x2="286" y2="68.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="278" y1="133.7" x2="286" y2="141.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="278" y1="141.7" x2="286" y2="133.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="312.7" y1="68.3" x2="320.7" y2="76.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="312.7" y1="76.3" x2="320.7" y2="68.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="312.7" y1="133.7" x2="320.7" y2="141.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="312.7" y1="141.7" x2="320.7" y2="133.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="18" y1="105" x2="105.7" y2="105" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="112,105 103.8,108.8 103.8,101.2" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="20" y="91" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">electron</text><text x="20" y="121" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">1.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹</text><line x1="120" y1="105" x2="350" y2="105" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:6 4"/><polygon points="356,105 348.7,108.4 348.7,101.6" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="120" y="198" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">E = 2.0 × 10³ V m⁻¹</text><line x1="120" y1="214" x2="128" y2="222" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="120" y1="222" x2="128" y2="214" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="136" y="218" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">B = ?</text></svg>', 'An electron moving at 1.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹ between plates giving an electric field of 2.0 × 10³ V m⁻¹; a magnetic field B between the plates cancels the deflection.'),
('29844196-6884-5d11-b63c-c0e5c96abc34', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 35, 35, 'In a velocity selector, which field does work on a particle that is being deflected?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Only the electric field', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The magnetic force is perpendicular to the velocity; the electric force can have a component along the motion. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: magnetic force perpendicular. C1: electric force can do work. A1: B (Only the electric field).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('3efe37f7-2f30-5d97-b34a-581035f09b9b', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 36, 36, 'Electrons pass undeflected through crossed fields of 3.0 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹ and 1.5 mT. The electric field is then switched off. Calculate the radius of their path in the magnetic field, in cm. Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C and mₑ = 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ kg.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '7.592 cm', 'cm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = E/B = 3.0 × 10⁴ ÷ 1.5 × 10⁻³ = 2.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹. r = mv/BQ = 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ × 2.0 × 10⁷ ÷ (1.5 × 10⁻³ × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 0.0759 m. In cm: 0.07592 × 100 = 7.59. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: v = E/B. C1: r = mv/BQ. C1: conversion. A1: r = 7.59 cm.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('e730f1b0-d6d9-56c8-9078-79683a241bdf', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 37, 37, 'In a selector, the top plate is positive, so the electric field points down the page. Positive ions move from left to right. Which magnetic field direction makes the magnetic force balance the electric force?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Into the page', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The electric force is downwards, so the magnetic force must be upwards: left-hand rule with current to the right and thumb up gives a field into the page. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: magnetic force must be upwards. C1: left-hand rule. A1: C (Into the page).', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 220" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgd3a7b2c4-t fgd3a7b2c4-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgd3a7b2c4-t">Selector plates</title><desc id="fgd3a7b2c4-d">Parallel plates with the top plate positive, so the electric field points down the page; positive ions enter from the left moving to the right. The magnetic field is not shown.</desc><rect x="90" y="42" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="90" y="170" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="78" y="46" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">+</text><text x="78" y="174" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">−</text><line x1="110" y1="56" x2="110" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="110,164 107,157.7 113,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="140" y1="56" x2="140" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="140,164 137,157.7 143,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="170" y1="56" x2="170" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="170,164 167,157.7 173,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="200" y1="56" x2="200" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="200,164 197,157.7 203,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="230" y1="56" x2="230" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="230,164 227,157.7 233,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="260" y1="56" x2="260" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="260,164 257,157.7 263,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="290" y1="56" x2="290" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="290,164 287,157.7 293,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="20" y1="110" x2="79.7" y2="110" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="86,110 77.8,113.8 77.8,106.2" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="22" y="96" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">positive ions</text><line x1="90" y1="110" x2="350" y2="110" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:6 4"/></svg>', 'Parallel plates with the top plate positive, so the electric field points down the page; positive ions enter from the left moving to the right. The magnetic field is not shown.'),
('6955263e-1a6b-5872-b3e0-fba1342a0a88', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 38, 38, 'Electrons emerge undeflected from crossed fields of 1.0 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹ and 2.0 × 10⁻³ T. What kinetic energy, in eV, do they have? Take mₑ = 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ kg and e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '71.17', 'eV', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = E/B = 1.0 × 10⁴ ÷ 2.0 × 10⁻³ = 5.0 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹. E_k = 0.5 × 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ × (5.0 × 10⁶)² = 1.14 × 10⁻¹⁷ J. In eV: 1.139 × 10⁻¹⁷ ÷ 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 71.2. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: v = E/B. C1: E_k in eV. A1: E_k = 71.2 eV.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('98f8e80b-329b-5aaf-8762-cfdab083e09c', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 39, 39, 'A selector uses B = 0.30 T and plates 2.0 cm apart. Calculate the p.d. needed to select particles moving at 2.0 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1200', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'V = Ed = Bvd = 0.30 × 2.0 × 10⁵ × 0.020 = 1200 V. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: E = Bv. C1: V = Ed. A1: V = 1200 V.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 440 222" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgfd5f0d39-t fgfd5f0d39-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgfd5f0d39-t">Velocity selector</title><desc id="fgfd5f0d39-d">A velocity selector with plates 2.0 cm apart and a 0.30 T magnetic field into the page, selecting particles moving at 2.0 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹.</desc><rect x="120" y="42" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="120" y="160" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="108" y="46" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">+</text><text x="108" y="164" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">−</text><line x1="139.3" y1="68.3" x2="147.3" y2="76.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="139.3" y1="76.3" x2="147.3" y2="68.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="139.3" y1="133.7" x2="147.3" y2="141.7" style="stroke:v