('4d0c566d-4616-56d2-a5c8-32c3a660d150', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 40, 40, 'For a particle moving faster than E/B through a velocity selector, which statement is correct?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The magnetic force is larger than the electric force', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'BQv grows with v; EQ does not. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: F_B ∝ v. C1: F_B > F_E. A1: A (The magnetic force is larger than the electric force).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('f70ccd75-1e3d-535d-8405-be043535d908', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 41, 41, 'In a velocity selector, E = 4.0 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹ with an uncertainty of ±2 % and B = 0.080 T with an uncertainty of ±1 %. Calculate the percentage uncertainty in the selected speed.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3', '%', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = E/B, so the percentage uncertainties add: 2 + 1 = 3.0 %. Mark scheme (4 marks). M1: quotient rule. C1: add percentages. C1: value. A1: uncertainty = 3.0%.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('a89b7e0c-1d3f-5acc-b4d9-bb1a921e0722', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 42, 42, 'A velocity selector with B = 0.010 T must select particles moving at 1.0 % of the speed of light. Calculate the electric field needed. Take c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '30000', 'V m⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = 0.010 × 3.00 × 10⁸ = 3.0 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹. E = Bv = 0.010 × 3.0 × 10⁶ = 3.0 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: v. C1: E = Bv. A1: E = 3.0 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('911f6bd1-fea5-54c2-8300-d383750f805d', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 43, 43, 'Electrons accelerated through 2.5 kV pass undeflected between plates 1.5 cm apart with a p.d. of 450 V, in a magnetic field of 1.0 mT. (a) Calculate the electric field. (b) Calculate the speed of the electrons from the crossed fields. (c) Check this speed using the accelerating p.d. and e/m = 1.76 × 10¹¹ C kg⁻¹. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3e7', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) E = 450 ÷ 0.015 = 3.0 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹. (b) v = E/B = 3.0 × 10⁴ ÷ 1.0 × 10⁻³ = 3.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹. (c) v = √(2(e/m)V) = √(2 × 1.76 × 10¹¹ × 2500) = 2.97 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹, in good agreement. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: E = V/d. M1: EQ = BQv. C1: v = E/B. C1: speed from energy. B1: agreement. A1: v = 3.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 440 242" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgcc2beb9d-t fgcc2beb9d-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgcc2beb9d-t">Crossed fields</title><desc id="fgcc2beb9d-d">Electrons accelerated through 2.5 kV pass undeflected between plates 1.5 cm apart with a p.d. of 450 V, in a magnetic field of 1.0 mT.</desc><rect x="120" y="42" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="120" y="160" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="108" y="46" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">+</text><text x="108" y="164" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentCo