('09e88407-e6f1-5fb8-a26c-936b04ba80a9', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 44, 44, 'Singly charged ²⁰Ne⁺ and ²²Ne⁺ ions (masses 3.32 × 10⁻²⁶ kg and 3.65 × 10⁻²⁶ kg) pass through a velocity selector with E = 2.0 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹ and B₁ = 0.10 T, then enter a field B₂ = 0.20 T and travel through a semicircle. (a) Calculate the speed of the ions leaving the selector. (b) Calculate the radius for each isotope. (c) Calculate the separation of the two images, in cm. Give only the answer to (c). Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '4.125 cm', 'cm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) v = 2.0 × 10⁴ ÷ 0.10 = 2.0 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹. (b) r₂₀ = 3.32 × 10⁻²⁶ × 2.0 × 10⁵ ÷ (1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 0.20) = 0.208 m; r₂₂ = 3.65 × 10⁻²⁶ × 2.0 × 10⁵ ÷ (1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 0.20) = 0.228 m. (c) Separation = 2 × (0.2281 − 0.2075) = 0.0413 m. In cm: 0.04125 × 100 = 4.12. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: v = E/B₁. C1: r₂₀. C1: r₂₂. M1: separation = 2Δr. C1: conversion. A1: Δx = 4.13 cm.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 260" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg964516ba-t fg964516ba-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg964516ba-t">Neon isotopes</title><desc id="fg964516ba-d">Singly charged ²⁰Ne⁺ and ²²Ne⁺ ions leave a velocity selector (E = 2.0 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹, B₁ = 0.10 T) at the same speed and enter a field B₂ = 0.20 T, travelling semicircles to the detector.</desc><rect x="60" y="20" width="340" height="180" rx="0" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/><circle cx="77" cy="38" r="4.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="77" cy="38" r="1.6" style="