('a50abda8-46e6-547e-aa3f-dae83f3e5d70', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 45, 45, 'A velocity selector has E = 1.5 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹ and B = 0.050 T. A proton enters at 2.0 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹. (a) Calculate the selected speed. (b) Calculate the resultant force on the proton, in units of 10⁻¹⁶ N. (c) State the direction of the resultant force. Give only the answer to (b). Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '8', '10⁻¹⁶ N', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) v = 1.5 × 10⁴ ÷ 0.050 = 3.0 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹. (b) F = e(E − vB) = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × (1.5 × 10⁴ − 2.0 × 10⁵ × 0.050) = 8.00 × 10⁻¹⁶ N. (c) In the direction of the electric force, because the proton is slower than the selected speed. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: selected speed. M1: F = e(E − vB). C1: value. B1: direction of electric force. A1: F = 8.0 × 10⁻¹⁶ N.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 440 242" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg6291c048-t fg6291c048-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg6291c048-t">Velocity selector</title><desc id="fg6291c048-d">A velocity selector with E = 1.5 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹ and B = 0.050 T into the page; a proton enters from the left at 2.0 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹.</desc><rect x="120" y="42" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="120" y="160" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="108" y="46" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">+</text><text x="108" y="164" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:curre