olygon points="112,105 103.8,108.8 103.8,101.2" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="20" y="91" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">proton</text><text x="20" y="121" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">2.0 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹</text><text x="120" y="198" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">E = 1.5 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹</text><line x1="120" y1="214" x2="128" y2="222" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="120" y1="222" x2="128" y2="214" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="136" y="218" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">B = 0.050 T</text></svg>', 'A velocity selector with E = 1.5 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹ and B = 0.050 T into the page; a proton enters from the left at 2.0 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹.'),
('a1c80bb3-a951-5258-a158-54d6fba07e11', '3fd36cc2-d7e7-4424-b4b5-11a4a8b7ac04', '939a9c6c-194e-484e-83e2-0ab494ffa0d4', 'a-level', '25.3', '9702 coursebook 25.3 · Electric and magnetic fields', 46, 46, 'Electrons moving at 2.4 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹ pass between plates 5.0 cm long where E = 1.2 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹. (a) Calculate their deflection on leaving the plates with no magnetic field. (b) Calculate the magnetic flux density needed to cancel the deflection, in mT. (c) State the direction of this field relative to E and v. Give only the answer to (b). Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C and mₑ = 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ kg.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.5 mT', 'mT', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) a = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 1.2 × 10⁴ ÷ 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ = 2.11 × 10¹⁵ m s⁻²; t = 0.050 ÷ 2.4 × 10⁷ = 2.08 × 10⁻⁹ s; y = 0.5 × 2.108 × 10¹⁵ × (2.083 × 10⁻⁹)² = 0.00457 m. (b) B = E/v = 1.2 × 10⁴ ÷ 2.4 × 10⁷ = 5.0 × 10⁻⁴ T. In mT: 5.0 × 10⁻⁴ × 1000 = 0.50. (c) At right angles to both E and v. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: acceleration. C1: deflection. M1: B = E/v. C1: conversion. B1: mutually perpendicular. A1: B = 0.50 mT.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 220" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgbccbbcf3-t fgbccbbcf3-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgbccbbcf3-t">Electrons between plates</title><desc id="fgbccbbcf3-d">Electrons moving at 2.4 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹ enter midway between plates 5.0 cm long with a field of 1.2 × 10⁴ V m⁻¹ and are deflected towards the positive plate.</desc><rect x="90" y="42" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="90" y="170" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="78" y="46" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" d